<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Claus von Stauffenberg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1907">1907</a>–<a href="/years/1944">1944</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Claus von Stauffenberg was a German army officer who led the 20 July plot of 1944 against Hitler. Badly wounded in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>, he became chief of staff of the Replacement Army and placed a bomb in a briefcase at a conference at Hitler's Wolf's Lair headquarters in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-prussia">East Prussia</a>. Hitler survived, the coup in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/berlin">Berlin</a> collapsed, and Stauffenberg was shot that night.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/claus-von-stauffenberg.jpg" alt="Claus von Stauffenberg" width="320" height="426" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Claus_von_Stauffenberg_Portrait_Photograph.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
